2. Predefined Forms
Oracle provides predefined forms when an FCCS application is created. Their availability depends on the features enabled.

Examples include Balance Sheet, Income Statement, and Cash Flow forms.
Form	Purpose
FCCS_Balance Sheet by Consolidation	Review balances by consolidation status
FCCS_Balance Sheet by Movement Detail	Review account movements
FCCS_Balance Sheet by Period	Review balances across periods
FCCS_Cash Flow Period by Entity	Review cash flow by entity
FCCS_Monthly Cash Flow by Entity	Review monthly cash flow
FCCS_Quarterly Cash Flow by Entity	Review quarterly cash flow

Oracle specifies that the Service Administrator and Power User have Modify access to these forms by default. Users and Viewers can launch them but cannot modify their layouts.

When Basic Balance Sheet is selected during application creation, the Balance Sheet, Cash Flow, and Income Statement form folders are excluded.

