3. Form Components
A form has four principal layout areas.
POV: Actual · FY26 · India

Page Axis: Currency selection

Rows / Account	Jan	Feb	Mar
Revenue	500	550	600
Expenses	300	320	340
Profit	200	230	260

Illustrative form layout using fictional amounts.
Component	Function
Rows	Display selected members vertically
Columns	Display selected members horizontally
POV	Identifies members used for retrieving the data
Page Axis	Allows switching between selected page members

Important design considerations
Oracle describes several rules:
- Access permissions determine which form data a user can view or modify.
- In multicurrency applications, the selected Currency member determines the displayed currency.
- Level 0 members support data entry; parent-member intersections described in the guide are read-only.
- Shared members must be selected using supported relationship functions; entered values are stored against their base members.
- Using relationships such as Children or Descendants can simplify form maintenance and calculations.
