10. Best Practices for Forms with Validation Rules
Oracle provides specific performance recommendations.
Recommendation	Reason
Dense dimensions on rows and columns	Improve retrieval and validation efficiency
Sparse dimensions on Page Axis and POV	Reduce unnecessary grid complexity
Limit dimensions per row	Avoid excessive calculation work
Use Suppress Missing Blocks when appropriate	Improve performance for sparse rows
Reduce Run on Save rules	Limit work triggered by form saves
Prefer member formulas where appropriate	Avoid unnecessary formula columns
Limit forms to approximately 100 rows	Reduce form complexity
Use member functions	Reduce maintenance
Use user and substitution variables	Avoid creating excessive forms
Organize forms into folders	Improve management

These are recommendations, not universal requirements. Oracle advises testing performance-sensitive settings.

