Form precision determines how many decimal places appear in a cell.

Oracle distinguishes minimum and maximum precision.
Stored value	Precision configuration	Display
100	Minimum 3	100.000
100.12345	Maximum 3	100.123
100.12345	Maximum 0	100
100	Minimum 2	100.00

These are examples from Oracle's precision table.

Important: Precision changes how values are displayed, not the underlying stored values.
Procedure
