12. Asymmetric Rows and Columns
Definition: Asymmetric rows or columns contain different member selections from the same dimensions.

Oracle gives this example:
Segment	Scenario	Period
A	Actual	Q1
B	Budget	Q2, Q3, Q4

Procedure
1. Open the form and select Layout.
2. Use Dimension Selector to choose the dimension.
3. Open Member Selector.
4. Configure different member selections for the relevant row or column segments.
5. Click Save or Finish.
Why it matters: You can design comparison forms where different segments display different scenarios or periods.

