17. Enabling Year-to-Date Data Input
Definition: YTD Data Input allows eligible users to enter Year-to-Date data directly through the FCCS_YTD member in a form.

Oracle describes this functionality for Dense/Sparse Optimized (DSO) applications.
Procedure
1. Create or open the required form.
2. Select Actions → Edit.
3. Open Layout.
4. Ensure View is on POV or Page, not Rows or Columns.
5. Under Grid Properties → Other, enable YTD Data Input.
6. Save the form.
7. Reopen it and test eligible YTD intersections.
Oracle explains that the PostFormSave business rule supports this process.

The job is triggered on form save, but its YTD processing occurs only when the feature is enabled and YTD data is entered.
Security considerations
The guide describes special YTD security behavior involving FCCS_YTD and FCCS_YTD_Input.

It also specifies application-setting requirements for eligible User-role data entry.

Important: YTD input is not simply changing the displayed View member. It involves a specific input feature, processing rule, and security behavior.

