19. Working with Smart Lists
Definition: Smart Lists allow administrators to create custom dropdown lists that users select from cells in forms.

Instead of typing a value, users select one of the configured entries.
Practical example
A fictional finance form contains a review-status field.
Illustrative Smart List
Review Status
Pending


Selected value: Pending. This is an interactive illustration, not a connected FCCS application.

Creating a Smart List
1. Open Navigator → Create and Manage → Smart List.
2. Click Create.
3. Enter a unique Smart List name.
4. Click OK.
5. Open the Smart List and configure Properties.
6. Select Entries.
7. Add the dropdown items.
8. Save and preview.
Smart List entry properties
Property	Purpose
ID	Unique numeric identifier
Name	Internal entry name
Label	Text displayed to users

Oracle also describes automatically generating IDs.
Important Smart List topics
- Smart List properties and access requirements.
- Mapping Smart Lists to dimension members.
- Synchronizing Smart Lists with reporting applications.
- Adding, editing, and deleting entries.
- Previewing Smart Lists.
- Displaying #MISSING or a custom label.
Smart List access levels
Oracle documents None, Display, Read, and Write as Minimum Access Required options for controlling which member-related entries are visible.
Smart List and #MISSING
Oracle allows administrators to display missing Smart List values as blank, #MISSING, or a configured label such as No Change.

Important: Deleting a Smart List also removes associated mappings with dimension members and reporting applications.

